# ====================================================================
# COMPOSITION WITH THE POSITION VIEWS (§3.6.2's two axes).
# The view axis selects by POSITION, the class axis by the
# NEXT BYTE, and at `pos == n` there is no next byte -- so
# the accept is the view's SCALAR one and is never class-
# indexed. A `\b`-terminated match at end of subject is
# exactly that case: out-of-subject counts as non-word,
# which is a property of the POSITION and of no byte.
# ====================================================================

