# ====================================================================
# THE ENG_ATTEMPT HALF. A `^` routes the pattern to the
# computed-goto engine, whose accept is BAKED INTO THE LABEL
# BODY rather than read from an array -- so §3.6's table and
# §3.8's seed both take a different emitted shape there, and
# a corpus with no `^` cells would exercise neither.
# ====================================================================

# THREE ANCHORED CELLS ARE ABSENT FROM THIS BLOCK, and the
# omission is recorded rather than silent. `^\Bfoo`, `^\Bo`
# and `^a\bb` are patterns that can NEVER match -- their whole
# DFA is one dead state -- and pcrec answers them correctly, but
# the C it emits for that shape does not survive `-Wall -Wextra
# -Werror`: gcc inlines the always-returns-0 `<prefix>_search`
# into `<prefix>_match` and then reports the wrapper's `caps`
# array as maybe-uninitialized, even though the `found != 1`
# short-circuit means it is never read.
#
# IT IS NOT THIS WAVE'S DEFECT. The base-tier pattern `^a^b`
# reproduces it exactly on the pre-wave compiler (measured at
# c23662e), with no module enabled -- the class is 'an anchored
# pattern whose machine is entirely dead', and `\b`/`\B` merely
# add three new spellings that reach it. The cells below are the
# LIVE anchored equivalents, chosen so the ENG_ATTEMPT half of
# this corpus loses no coverage; the three absent ones go back
# the day the wrapper's warning is fixed.
